1
00:00:06,083 --> 00:00:09,000
Big Sis, Sir Tooka...

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:11,000
Lis.

3
00:00:11,041 --> 00:00:12,208
Remember what Sir Tooka said?

4
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:16,125
He has the best chance
of survival in this situation.

5
00:00:16,125 --> 00:00:18,208
Sir Tooka would never lie without reason.

6
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:23,083
I'm sure that he'll come back with Eve.

7
00:00:24,166 --> 00:00:27,041
My throat... I can't speak...

8
00:00:28,208 --> 00:00:33,000
This thing can still move,
even after eating my Stage Two?

9
00:00:33,166 --> 00:00:35,166
Her precision is growing with every thrust.

10
00:00:35,166 --> 00:00:38,125
She's the type to mature
in real combat, is she?!

11
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:42,000
Found it.

12
00:00:42,041 --> 00:00:43,000
Oh no!

13
00:00:43,166 --> 00:00:44,166
Itsuki.

14
00:00:46,125 --> 00:00:48,083
I've been waiting for you, Sis.

15
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:51,041
I see Kashima-san's safe.

16
00:00:51,208 --> 00:00:54,041
Well, it was a pretty close call.

17
00:00:54,166 --> 00:00:55,166
Sis...

18
00:00:56,041 --> 00:00:59,125
Can I ask why you stopped me
from delivering the final blow?

19
00:01:00,083 --> 00:01:01,208
That isn't a monster.

20
00:01:01,208 --> 00:01:02,166
Huh?

21
00:01:02,208 --> 00:01:05,083
Her disposition isn't like those
we've fought thus far.

22
00:01:05,083 --> 00:01:06,208
A lioness, huh?

23
00:01:06,208 --> 00:01:07,208
A leopard.

24
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:08,208
Huh?

25
00:01:09,083 --> 00:01:10,125
A leopard.

26
00:01:10,125 --> 00:01:13,083
So, like, does it make any difference?

27
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:17,083
What sets her apart
from a monster is her intelligence.

28
00:01:17,208 --> 00:01:20,083
The will in her eyes
and the way she carries herself

29
00:01:20,125 --> 00:01:22,208
actually strike me as closer to human.

30
00:01:22,208 --> 00:01:25,041
Meaning... what, exactly?

31
00:01:25,083 --> 00:01:28,000
We can most likely communicate
in earnest with her.

32
00:01:28,041 --> 00:01:30,125
But it doesn't seem like she can talk.

33
00:01:30,166 --> 00:01:33,000
It seems you disabled
her voice with your attack.

34
00:01:33,041 --> 00:01:35,083
Wait, I did? Did I screw up?

35
00:01:35,083 --> 00:01:37,041
Shit, I did...

36
00:01:37,041 --> 00:01:38,166
I messed up big-time.

37
00:01:38,208 --> 00:01:41,208
First, allow me to apologize
for my younger sister.

38
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:43,208
She tends to jump the gun,

39
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:47,125
and she prioritized my orders such
that she rushed in recklessly.

40
00:01:47,166 --> 00:01:49,041
I-I-I'm sorry.

41
00:01:49,041 --> 00:01:52,125
I have a habit of leaping to action
when my sister's not around.

42
00:01:52,166 --> 00:01:54,000
That said, my instructions were lacking.

43
00:01:54,041 --> 00:01:55,125
- That said, my instructions were lacking.
- She seems reasonable,
but she's got her guard up.

44
00:01:55,125 --> 00:01:56,083
- Now, I'd like to ask you a few questions.
- She seems reasonable,
but she's got her guard up.

45
00:01:56,125 --> 00:01:57,125
Now, I'd like to ask you a few questions.

46
00:01:57,166 --> 00:01:59,083
I know you still can't talk,
so could I ask you to answer with gestures?

47
00:01:59,125 --> 00:02:01,083
- I know you still can't talk,
so could I ask you to answer with gestures?
- This feeling...

48
00:02:01,083 --> 00:02:02,041
- I know you still can't talk,
so could I ask you to answer with gestures?
- It's different...

49
00:02:02,083 --> 00:02:04,125
Do you bear any hostility for the three of us?

50
00:02:04,208 --> 00:02:08,083
Then do you have any issue
with us all parting ways?

51
00:02:08,083 --> 00:02:10,208
But they remind me of Tooka.

52
00:02:14,208 --> 00:02:16,208
Who is this woman?

53
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:20,000
Hijiri Takao. That's my name.

54
00:02:20,083 --> 00:02:22,083
We're humans from another world.

55
00:02:22,208 --> 00:02:24,083
Why identify yourself...?

56
00:02:24,083 --> 00:02:25,125
She spoke!

57
00:02:25,125 --> 00:02:27,125
- Thank goodness!
- A show of courtesy...

58
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:30,208
- If she never spoke again,
I'd be racked with guilt forever!
- Eve Speed.

59
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:33,083
Quick to let your reactions
show on your face, are you?

60
00:02:34,125 --> 00:02:40,083
I heard the rumors of a leopardman
bloodsport warrior who went missing.

61
00:02:40,083 --> 00:02:42,166
You... aren't alone, are you?

62
00:02:42,208 --> 00:02:46,125
Perhaps you're searching for someone
you've been separated from.

63
00:02:46,166 --> 00:02:48,000
Exactly.

64
00:02:48,041 --> 00:02:50,125
I'm looking for my liege.

65
00:02:51,041 --> 00:02:54,166
If you're so intent on finding them,

66
00:02:54,208 --> 00:02:59,000
that suggests you anticipate that
they weathered the monster stampede, yes?

67
00:02:59,041 --> 00:03:05,083
Meaning your liege possesses the ability to
survive an encounter with human-faced beasts.

68
00:03:06,125 --> 00:03:09,000
Your insight is stunning.

69
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:14,000
However, my liege cannot be
gauged by such a simple measure.

70
00:03:14,125 --> 00:03:16,208
Now I'm even more intrigued.

71
00:03:20,083 --> 00:03:21,125
Paralyze!

72
00:03:21,125 --> 00:03:24,208
Berserk! Berserk! Berserk!

73
00:03:30,041 --> 00:03:31,041
Piggymaru!

74
00:03:36,083 --> 00:03:37,125
Sleep!

75
00:03:42,166 --> 00:03:44,000
Poison!

76
00:03:49,083 --> 00:03:51,083
TOOKA MIMORI
- I still have MP in reserve.

77
00:03:51,083 --> 00:03:53,125
But Piggymaru's...

78
00:03:54,083 --> 00:03:55,166
You did a great job.

79
00:04:02,041 --> 00:04:04,166
I bet you're well past your limit, too.

80
00:04:04,208 --> 00:04:08,041
If you really feel yourself hitting it,
let me know. Don't hide it.

81
00:04:08,083 --> 00:04:10,041
I'll handle the rest from there.

82
00:04:10,208 --> 00:04:12,000
Once we part ways,

83
00:04:12,041 --> 00:04:13,208
I'll leave Seras and the others to you.

84
00:04:18,125 --> 00:04:20,125
Must've gotten banged up in that fall..

85
00:04:22,166 --> 00:04:24,166
Still, I've made it this far.

86
00:04:27,166 --> 00:04:29,041
Status: Open.

87
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:32,083
TOOKA MIMORI
E-CLASS HERO
- I've even reached Level 2,000.

88
00:04:32,083 --> 00:04:34,000
TOOKA MIMORI
E-CLASS HERO
- But my energy and wounds don't recover

89
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:35,166
TOOKA MIMORI
E-CLASS HERO
- no matter how high my values climb.

90
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:38,125
I'm starting to feel weak, too.

91
00:04:38,125 --> 00:04:39,125
Also...

92
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:41,125
There's one left.

93
00:04:41,166 --> 00:04:43,083
Most likely a human-faced beast.

94
00:04:44,041 --> 00:04:46,000
You've been watching all this time, right?

95
00:04:46,083 --> 00:04:49,000
I can't inflict anything on it
without line of sight.

96
00:04:49,041 --> 00:04:52,083
That's the most crucial condition
to activating my status ailment skill.

97
00:04:53,041 --> 00:04:56,208
And this last human-faced beast
has picked up on that.

98
00:04:57,083 --> 00:04:59,041
This is the final stage of our battle.

99
00:05:03,166 --> 00:05:07,125
RULER AND SWORD

100
00:05:08,041 --> 00:05:09,041
Slei!

101
00:05:47,166 --> 00:05:49,000
Piggymaru...

102
00:05:49,208 --> 00:05:53,041
Sorry, but could I ask you
to do one last job for me?

103
00:06:31,125 --> 00:06:32,125
Paralyze!

104
00:06:33,041 --> 00:06:34,125
Your real target is above you!

105
00:06:36,125 --> 00:06:37,125
Berserk!

106
00:06:44,166 --> 00:06:46,041
Yeah, that's right.

107
00:06:47,166 --> 00:06:51,083
I used my mask as a decoy
and made you think,

108
00:06:51,166 --> 00:06:55,125
"This is a trap. He's going to flank me."

109
00:06:56,000 --> 00:06:58,083
Then, while you were distracted by Piggymaru,

110
00:06:58,125 --> 00:07:00,083
I leapt into the air

111
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:03,041
so I could get a full view of you.

112
00:07:04,000 --> 00:07:07,000
You were preventing me from
using my skill by hiding yourself,

113
00:07:07,041 --> 00:07:09,083
except that also meant...

114
00:07:09,083 --> 00:07:11,125
you couldn't see me either.

115
00:07:15,166 --> 00:07:16,166
Status: Open.

116
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:19,208
TOOKA MIMORI
- I'm surprised I've hit critical.

117
00:07:24,166 --> 00:07:26,083
You have leveled up.

118
00:07:26,125 --> 00:07:28,208
Your Paralyze Skill has leveled up.

119
00:07:29,000 --> 00:07:31,041
An advanced skill has been unlocked.

120
00:07:31,041 --> 00:07:32,083
An advanced skill?

121
00:07:35,166 --> 00:07:37,166
Sorry for pushing you guys so hard.

122
00:07:38,083 --> 00:07:40,208
Now, shall we head back
to Seras and the others?

123
00:07:43,041 --> 00:07:45,000
My legs are in bad shape.

124
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:51,166
I have plenty of MP.

125
00:07:52,083 --> 00:07:54,125
It'll all come down to my stamina.

126
00:07:57,041 --> 00:07:58,041
Par—

127
00:08:02,083 --> 00:08:03,125
Ah...

128
00:08:04,083 --> 00:08:07,000
I had a feeling this might happen.

129
00:08:07,166 --> 00:08:10,166
I've found you, my liege.

130
00:08:12,166 --> 00:08:16,083
I get Slei and Piggymaru, but me too?

131
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:19,208
My strength is one of my best assets.

132
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:21,125
While I was searching for you,

133
00:08:21,125 --> 00:08:23,083
I encountered heroes from another world.

134
00:08:23,083 --> 00:08:27,083
Hijiri Takao, Itsuki, and
another girl called Kashima.

135
00:08:27,166 --> 00:08:29,125
The Takao sisters and Kashima, huh?

136
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:31,083
And what of my name?

137
00:08:31,083 --> 00:08:32,125
I did not give it.

138
00:08:32,125 --> 00:08:35,000
I didn't know what their
relationship with you was like.

139
00:08:35,041 --> 00:08:37,041
Yeah, good call.

140
00:08:37,166 --> 00:08:40,041
It's best if Mimori Touka stays dead to them.

141
00:08:40,208 --> 00:08:45,000
It's easy to imagine the 2-C heroes becoming
an obstacle to my revenge on the goddess.

142
00:08:45,041 --> 00:08:49,083
Your mind is still turning even when
you're gravely injured, isn't it?

143
00:08:49,125 --> 00:08:54,083
I'd honestly love to find somewhere
we can take a break, though.

144
00:08:57,166 --> 00:08:59,041
Slei?

145
00:08:59,208 --> 00:09:00,166
And...

146
00:09:01,125 --> 00:09:03,000
Sir Tooka!

147
00:09:03,125 --> 00:09:05,166
Big Sis! Sir Tooka!

148
00:09:05,208 --> 00:09:07,208
Little Slei and Piggymaru!

149
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:09,083
Big Sis!

150
00:09:09,208 --> 00:09:12,041
I came back alive, just as I promised.

151
00:09:12,083 --> 00:09:13,083
Ahem.

152
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:15,041
Sir Tooka,

153
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:17,125
I'm glad to see you safe.

154
00:09:18,083 --> 00:09:21,208
Seras, could you check on Slei for me?

155
00:09:29,083 --> 00:09:32,041
Well then, I'll go stand watch.

156
00:09:32,041 --> 00:09:33,125
Sorry.

157
00:09:33,166 --> 00:09:35,125
I know you're probably tired too.

158
00:09:36,041 --> 00:09:39,083
My fatigue is nothing compared to yours.

159
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:41,083
I'm done.

160
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:44,125
You're able to tend wounds,
and you can wield a sword.

161
00:09:44,166 --> 00:09:46,000
I couldn't ask for more.

162
00:09:47,041 --> 00:09:49,166
I also know how to sew.

163
00:09:49,166 --> 00:09:50,125
I'd appreciate it.

164
00:09:50,166 --> 00:09:51,125
Leave it to me.

165
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:56,125
You can't sleep?

166
00:09:57,041 --> 00:10:00,000
Guess I'm still too on edge for that.

167
00:10:00,041 --> 00:10:02,208
But even so, just lying down
is an improvement.

168
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:09,000
Well, I'm not sure if this well help
calm your nerves or not, but...

169
00:10:09,000 --> 00:10:10,000
Get some sleep.

170
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:14,125
Um, to be honest, I'm tense too,
so I don't feel like I could rest.

171
00:10:14,125 --> 00:10:16,208
I get it. She's just pretending right now.

172
00:10:18,083 --> 00:10:20,000
Then I'll take you up on that.

173
00:10:21,166 --> 00:10:25,208
I haven't really slept in someone's lap
since my aunt let me do it ages ago.

174
00:10:29,166 --> 00:10:30,208
Seras?

175
00:10:31,083 --> 00:10:34,041
Please don't carry everything
all by yourself.

176
00:10:35,208 --> 00:10:38,083
Did I look that worn down?

177
00:10:38,083 --> 00:10:41,208
Even when all the creatures in this
Land of Monsters beset us at once,

178
00:10:41,208 --> 00:10:45,125
you put on a brave face and acted
as if it were nothing to you.

179
00:10:47,000 --> 00:10:51,041
Eve and Lis were reassured to see it, but...

180
00:10:51,041 --> 00:10:53,125
I guess you could sense the lies mixed in.

181
00:10:53,125 --> 00:10:54,125
Yes.

182
00:10:56,083 --> 00:10:58,125
Sometimes I get scared.

183
00:10:58,125 --> 00:11:01,208
Scared that one day you'll charge
yourself with a task too heavy

184
00:11:02,000 --> 00:11:04,166
and you'll suddenly fall apart.

185
00:11:04,208 --> 00:11:06,166
That worries me.

186
00:11:08,083 --> 00:11:09,083
Seras.

187
00:11:10,041 --> 00:11:12,166
If you insist on worrying about me,

188
00:11:12,166 --> 00:11:15,125
then support me as best you
can so that doesn't happen.

189
00:11:17,083 --> 00:11:18,041
Yes.

190
00:11:18,041 --> 00:11:21,166
Trust that I will, Sir Tooka.

191
00:11:23,166 --> 00:11:26,166
- I'll kill you, brat!
- I've been regaining the Touka I was back then.

192
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:30,083
- Just try and break me if you can!
- Had I stayed the "normal"
person I became over time,

193
00:11:30,125 --> 00:11:33,041
I'm sure this world would've
broken me long ago.

194
00:11:34,166 --> 00:11:36,000
So for now...

195
00:11:36,125 --> 00:11:38,000
this is fine.

196
00:11:39,166 --> 00:11:43,208
However, please come to me without reservation
whenever it becomes hard for you.

197
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:45,166
If there's anything I can do to help,

198
00:11:45,166 --> 00:11:48,000
I'll happily oblige however I can.

199
00:11:49,125 --> 00:11:51,166
You're such an overprotective vice captain.

200
00:11:52,208 --> 00:11:56,000
I would rather you say I'm devoted.

201
00:11:57,041 --> 00:11:59,125
Maybe this is what it's like
to have an older sister.

202
00:12:00,125 --> 00:12:03,083
Speaking of, Sir Tooka, how old are you?

203
00:12:03,125 --> 00:12:05,125
Hmm? I'm seventeen.

204
00:12:05,166 --> 00:12:08,041
What? You're younger than me?

205
00:12:08,083 --> 00:12:09,208
Well, of course I am.

206
00:12:09,208 --> 00:12:12,000
High elves are longer-lived
than humans, right?

207
00:12:12,083 --> 00:12:13,083
Nineteen.

208
00:12:14,166 --> 00:12:16,083
Is that your age?

209
00:12:17,041 --> 00:12:20,041
I was convinced you must've
lived for a century or so.

210
00:12:20,083 --> 00:12:21,041
Wait, hold on.

211
00:12:21,041 --> 00:12:22,208
How old did you think I was?

212
00:12:23,000 --> 00:12:25,208
I thought you were in your
early or mid-twenties.

213
00:12:25,208 --> 00:12:29,125
Um, you're just so calm about everything.

214
00:12:29,125 --> 00:12:30,166
I see.

215
00:12:31,208 --> 00:12:35,041
There's so much I still don't
know about you, isn't there?

216
00:12:35,041 --> 00:12:36,166
I could say the same.

217
00:12:36,208 --> 00:12:40,083
So, do you plan on treating me
like a younger brother now?

218
00:12:40,083 --> 00:12:44,083
No, you are the ruler of the
Lord of the Flies' War Band.

219
00:12:44,083 --> 00:12:45,166
Even if you're younger than me,

220
00:12:45,208 --> 00:12:49,208
I shall not regard the ruler
I swore loyalty to any differently.

221
00:12:49,208 --> 00:12:53,000
I'm not really fit to be a ruler, you know?

222
00:12:53,000 --> 00:12:54,125
No, Sir Tooka.

223
00:12:54,166 --> 00:12:58,166
You are my dear, one and only
ruler right now.

224
00:12:59,083 --> 00:13:00,083
I see...

225
00:13:07,041 --> 00:13:08,041
Sir Tooka?

226
00:13:08,125 --> 00:13:11,041
Have you fallen asleep already?

227
00:13:11,166 --> 00:13:14,083
Truly, you were utterly worn out, weren't you?

228
00:13:14,208 --> 00:13:16,000
Sir Tooka...

229
00:13:22,125 --> 00:13:26,166
So this is what Sir Tooka looks
like when he's acting his age...

230
00:13:28,125 --> 00:13:31,166
I never thought I would feel
this way for someone.

231
00:13:32,125 --> 00:13:33,125
So this is...

232
00:13:37,083 --> 00:13:38,125
Sir Tooka?

233
00:14:01,083 --> 00:14:03,041
Sir Tooka...

234
00:14:03,041 --> 00:14:04,041
This is...

235
00:14:26,041 --> 00:14:29,125
What... was I about to...

236
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:38,083
Hmm?

237
00:14:43,041 --> 00:14:44,041
Seras.

238
00:14:44,166 --> 00:14:46,083
You can't sleep?

239
00:14:46,083 --> 00:14:48,083
I'm terribly sorry.

240
00:14:49,000 --> 00:14:50,125
Why are you apologizing?

241
00:14:50,166 --> 00:14:52,166
F-Forgive me.

242
00:14:52,166 --> 00:14:54,125
Shall I use my skill to put you to sleep?

243
00:14:55,041 --> 00:14:56,166
Please.

244
00:14:57,041 --> 00:14:58,083
Sleep.

245
00:15:07,166 --> 00:15:09,041
I see...

246
00:15:10,041 --> 00:15:14,125
At some point, I started letting myself
be that vulnerable around you, huh?

247
00:15:15,208 --> 00:15:18,208
Once again, thank you very much, Takao-san.

248
00:15:19,000 --> 00:15:22,125
Whoa, you're super formal, Kashima.

249
00:15:22,166 --> 00:15:24,000
You can call me Itsuki.

250
00:15:24,041 --> 00:15:26,125
My sister and I are both Takaos, you know?

251
00:15:26,125 --> 00:15:29,000
By the way, I wanted to ask you something.

252
00:15:29,041 --> 00:15:31,125
S-Sure. What is it?

253
00:15:31,208 --> 00:15:34,041
Why are you in Asagi's group?

254
00:15:34,083 --> 00:15:35,041
Huh?

255
00:15:35,041 --> 00:15:37,166
You're way more like the class prez,
no matter how you cut it.

256
00:15:38,083 --> 00:15:39,208
Well, it's because...

257
00:15:40,083 --> 00:15:43,000
Man, I knew you couldn't do it.

258
00:15:43,083 --> 00:15:46,166
Good thing I'm here
for our timid little pigeon.

259
00:15:47,041 --> 00:15:48,166
Let me help you with that.

260
00:15:50,041 --> 00:15:51,166
Good job, little pigeon!

261
00:15:51,166 --> 00:15:54,166
You've passed the test,
and that settles things!

262
00:15:55,083 --> 00:15:58,125
Humanity has always survived
by joining hands, meow.

263
00:15:58,166 --> 00:16:01,041
But if we don't start helping
each other after joining up,

264
00:16:01,041 --> 00:16:03,083
then we end up crushing each other, woof.

265
00:16:03,166 --> 00:16:07,041
So we all need to look
after one another, cluck.

266
00:16:07,041 --> 00:16:12,125
Kobato-san, are you listening to me?

267
00:16:13,041 --> 00:16:16,166
So I'm going to stick with Asagi-san's group.

268
00:16:16,166 --> 00:16:20,125
Asagi's kinda got a dangerous
vibe though, you know?

269
00:16:20,125 --> 00:16:21,208
Yes, I know.

270
00:16:22,000 --> 00:16:25,208
And someday, that might
be what saves Sogou-san.

271
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:27,000
Huh?

272
00:16:38,166 --> 00:16:40,166
Um, Sir Tooka?

273
00:16:40,166 --> 00:16:41,125
What is it?

274
00:16:41,166 --> 00:16:45,166
There's something I'd like
to confess to you one day.

275
00:16:45,166 --> 00:16:47,041
"One day," huh?

276
00:16:47,083 --> 00:16:48,041
Yes.

277
00:16:48,041 --> 00:16:51,000
Right now I lack the courage to do so.

278
00:16:51,041 --> 00:16:55,000
So please give me some time.

279
00:16:55,208 --> 00:16:57,000
All right.

280
00:16:58,000 --> 00:17:02,125
I know it's unfair to make this so one-sided.

281
00:17:02,166 --> 00:17:07,125
But if I confess, then I
might lose Sir Tooka's trust.

282
00:17:07,166 --> 00:17:10,041
However, I have to tell him eventually,

283
00:17:10,041 --> 00:17:11,208
even if he curses me for it

284
00:17:12,083 --> 00:17:15,000
and even if it destroys
our current relationship.

285
00:17:15,125 --> 00:17:20,125
If Seras hasn't realized that I already know,
then things are fine as they are for now.

286
00:17:21,041 --> 00:17:23,208
I know Seras will eventually come clean.

287
00:17:24,000 --> 00:17:25,125
I'll tell him I love him,

288
00:17:25,166 --> 00:17:30,083
which terrifies me more
than crossing swords with any foe.

289
00:17:30,125 --> 00:17:32,041
So, Sir Tooka,

290
00:17:32,166 --> 00:17:36,083
please give me time to muster my courage.

291
00:17:36,166 --> 00:17:38,000
Until then...

292
00:17:38,083 --> 00:17:39,125
Until then...

293
00:17:40,000 --> 00:17:41,125
I will be my ruler's sword.

294
00:17:42,000 --> 00:17:44,125
I will play the role of Seras's liege.

295
00:17:46,125 --> 00:17:47,083
WITCH'S TERRITORY

296
00:17:47,125 --> 00:17:48,125
WITCH'S TERRITORY
- This is a magic seal.

297
00:17:48,125 --> 00:17:50,125
This is a magic seal.

298
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:54,125
Is it the kind that triggers
a trap under certain conditions?

299
00:17:54,125 --> 00:17:58,125
A portion of the formula is damaged,
so it probably won't activate.

300
00:17:58,166 --> 00:18:00,166
It looks rather old as well.

301
00:18:01,041 --> 00:18:02,083
It's old?

302
00:18:03,000 --> 00:18:06,000
I really hope we're not looking at a situation

303
00:18:06,041 --> 00:18:08,125
where the witch turns out to be dead already.

304
00:18:08,125 --> 00:18:10,041
What is that?

305
00:18:13,166 --> 00:18:15,083
Similar seals?

306
00:18:15,125 --> 00:18:17,083
Looks like this one's live.

307
00:18:25,083 --> 00:18:26,083
Paralyze!

308
00:18:28,000 --> 00:18:32,041
Well, it's probably a golem to welcome
invaders or something like that.

309
00:18:32,083 --> 00:18:34,083
Should we shatter it to be safe?

310
00:18:34,083 --> 00:18:36,166
No, I don't want to destroy stuff recklessly

311
00:18:36,208 --> 00:18:39,125
and make the witch think
we're hostile toward her.

312
00:18:44,041 --> 00:18:46,125
I can't believe I'm not
sensing a single monster.

313
00:18:46,125 --> 00:18:49,125
I guess we're definitely in the
witch's territory now.

314
00:19:03,000 --> 00:19:04,208
Are those golems too?

315
00:19:04,208 --> 00:19:06,166
Looks like I don't need my skill.

316
00:19:06,166 --> 00:19:08,125
They're just quietly working away.

317
00:19:09,208 --> 00:19:10,208
Tooka.

318
00:19:10,208 --> 00:19:14,041
I just hope it opens with
magic like we theorized.

319
00:19:15,166 --> 00:19:16,208
Now I see.

320
00:19:17,041 --> 00:19:20,083
The witch didn't bother to hide this thing

321
00:19:20,083 --> 00:19:23,083
because it consumes an
extraordinary amount of magic.

322
00:19:23,208 --> 00:19:26,208
However, my magic capacity
is one thing I'm confident in.

323
00:19:28,125 --> 00:19:29,125
Eve.

324
00:19:35,000 --> 00:19:36,083
Kashima-san!

325
00:19:37,208 --> 00:19:39,125
- Sogou—
- Little pigeon!

326
00:19:39,166 --> 00:19:41,083
I was so worried about you!

327
00:19:41,125 --> 00:19:43,083
Asagi-san, I'm sorry I worried you.

328
00:19:43,125 --> 00:19:46,041
So, why are you with the Takaos?

329
00:19:46,041 --> 00:19:48,166
We ran into each other,
and they helped me out.

330
00:19:48,166 --> 00:19:52,083
Huh. Guess the Takaos are pretty nice.

331
00:19:52,125 --> 00:19:53,125
Kashima-san.

332
00:19:55,041 --> 00:19:56,041
I'm glad...

333
00:19:56,166 --> 00:19:58,041
I'm so glad you're safe.

334
00:19:58,125 --> 00:20:00,041
Sogou-san...

335
00:20:01,083 --> 00:20:04,125
It's okay. Takao-san and her sister saved me.

336
00:20:04,166 --> 00:20:07,125
The Four Saints are still out looking for you,

337
00:20:07,125 --> 00:20:09,000
so I'll go tell them we've found you.

338
00:20:09,041 --> 00:20:10,041
O-Okay.

339
00:20:10,041 --> 00:20:13,208
Boy, am I glad all our allies
made it out unharmed.

340
00:20:16,000 --> 00:20:19,041
It's okay that I'm still a timid,
foolish pigeon for now.

341
00:20:19,125 --> 00:20:21,208
But I have to get stronger.

342
00:20:22,125 --> 00:20:25,208
Looks like we made the right call
to go search for Kashima-san.

343
00:20:26,166 --> 00:20:29,166
Those soldiers we found in the forest...

344
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:31,208
This is still only speculation,

345
00:20:31,208 --> 00:20:34,166
but I think their goal was
to assassinate the students of 2-C.

346
00:20:35,000 --> 00:20:37,166
And I'm not talking about
just one or two of us.

347
00:20:37,208 --> 00:20:39,083
What do you mean?

348
00:20:39,125 --> 00:20:41,125
If Kashima-san had died,

349
00:20:41,166 --> 00:20:44,125
it would have made a
terrible impact on Sogou-san.

350
00:20:44,166 --> 00:20:45,125
I see.

351
00:20:45,125 --> 00:20:47,166
If her heart were to break now,

352
00:20:49,166 --> 00:20:52,208
it's easy to imagine what would follow.

353
00:20:53,125 --> 00:20:56,041
That would be very boring.

354
00:20:57,000 --> 00:20:58,208
There's a sky underground?

355
00:20:59,000 --> 00:21:00,041
Incredible!

356
00:21:00,083 --> 00:21:02,166
Must be the power of magic.

357
00:21:03,000 --> 00:21:06,166
That, or we entered another space
after passing through the door.

358
00:21:08,041 --> 00:21:09,166
There's even a breeze.

359
00:21:23,125 --> 00:21:24,125
Tooka.

360
00:21:25,083 --> 00:21:26,041
Yeah.

361
00:21:26,125 --> 00:21:28,166
I'd wager that's...

362
00:21:29,083 --> 00:21:31,041
who we've been seeking.

363
00:21:31,125 --> 00:21:33,000
The Witch of Taboos.

364
00:21:33,000 --> 00:21:34,041
If the rumors are correct,

365
00:21:34,083 --> 00:21:38,041
she's the only one capable of deciphering
the scroll of forbidden magic.

366
00:21:39,041 --> 00:21:42,125
She'll be our only lead on how
to exact revenge upon the goddess.

367
00:21:42,125 --> 00:21:44,125
Send word to the Four Saints.

368
00:21:44,125 --> 00:21:47,000
The Great Demon Empire's
forces are on the move,

369
00:21:47,041 --> 00:21:50,041
- and they should recall the heroes at once.
- Ma'am!

370
00:21:50,041 --> 00:21:57,125
Now, I wonder how wounded and how much
stronger the heroes will be when they return...

371
00:21:58,041 --> 00:21:59,125
I can't wait to find out.

372
00:22:02,041 --> 00:22:05,041
- Now then, I wonder if you can
use the ancient language.
- It certainly wasn't an easy road to get here.

373
00:22:05,166 --> 00:22:08,125
- It was a cruel path that wore on our nerves.
- You mean this one?

374
00:22:08,125 --> 00:22:10,166
Nevertheless, we made it.

375
00:22:10,166 --> 00:22:12,041
Now this is where things start.

376
00:22:12,208 --> 00:22:14,125
Let me first introduce myself.

377
00:22:14,166 --> 00:22:16,041
My name is Erica Anaorovael.

378
00:22:16,041 --> 00:22:18,125
ERICA ANAOROVAEL
DARK ELF, WITCH OF TABOOS
- My name is Erica Anaorovael.

379
00:22:18,166 --> 00:22:21,166
I am indeed the one you
call the Witch of Taboos.

380
00:22:21,208 --> 00:22:23,166
Just you wait, Vicius...

381
00:22:25,166 --> 00:22:29,041
I'll annihilate everything of yours!

